        "severity": "awkward",
        "suggestion": "Add document.scope (classes or parts covered) and document.event_id so per-class pages of one event can be joined."
      },
      {
        "what": "NATC tie-breaks apply only to Pro down to 5th and to podium places in other classes (rule 8); tie_breaks has no scope, so the rule set over-claims for lower places.",
        "where": "rule_sets[natc].tie_breaks",
        "severity": "awkward",
        "suggestion": "Add rule_set.tie_break_scope (classes, ranks) or allow tie_breaks entries to carry applies_to."
      },
      {
        "what": "Rider Name is one upper-case field and the order is not consistent ('MURPHY AARON' appears family-first, the rest given-first), so given/family cannot be split with certainty.",
        "where": "entries[].people[].person.name",
        "severity": "cosmetic",
        "suggestion": "None needed; as_printed carries it. A name.order_uncertain flag would help consumers."
      },
      {
        "what": "Every Pro rider has 5 on all 12 sections of loop 3 (loop total 60) and the page gives no reason. If this was an official decision (loop abandoned and scored 5 for all), the protocol has no part-level way to say the marks were imposed rather than ridden.",
